          "heading": "Brittany Hogan double helps Ireland Women secure vital WXV win over Japan",
          "body": "Ireland Women recovered from their opening-round defeat to the USA with a hard-fought 31-24 victory against Japan in Galway. After squandering a significant lead last weekend, Scott Bemand’s side showed improved composure as Brittany Hogan crossed twice and Béibhinn Parsons claimed her record-breaking 24th international try. Despite a spirited second-half comeback from the visitors at Dexcom Stadium, Ireland’s defence held firm under pressure. Bemand said the side \"showed what we're about\" before they travel to face South Africa next."
