          "body": "Glasgow Warriors snatched a 26-20 victory over Munster at Thomond Park on Saturday, with a powerful bench performance driving a late turnaround. Trailing by 10 points at the interval, the visitors capitalised as the hosts fatigued in the final quarter. Nathan McBeth and George Horne were instrumental in the second half, with Horne crossing for the decisive scores to secure a bonus point. The result sees Glasgow open their United Rugby Championship campaign with a high-stakes away win."
